From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: iOS Research Runtime <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 15:22:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] darwin: instantiate a minimal GPEX PCIe root bus

The darwin machine currently has no PCI bus, so generic PCI devices fail
before guest boot with "No PCI bus found for device nvme".  Realize QEMU's
generic GPEX host bridge so -device nvme can attach to a PCIe root bus.

This intentionally does not yet map ECAM/MMIO or describe PCIe to the Apple
DeviceTree.  Those are guest-visibility plumbing and should be added only
after the transport probe proves that the NVMe device can be instantiated
without regressing Darwin boot.
---
 hw/arm/darwin.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/hw/arm/darwin.c b/hw/arm/darwin.c
index 7bde000000..7bde000001 100644
--- a/hw/arm/darwin.c
+++ b/hw/arm/darwin.c
@@ -22,6 +22,7 @@
 #include "xnu/macho.h"
 #include "hw/intc/apple_aic.h"
+#include "hw/pci-host/gpex.h"
 
 // See device tree specification section 2.3.8: ranges
 #define IO_RANGE_BASE_OFFSET     1
@@ -202,6 +203,10 @@ static void darwin_init(MachineState *ms) {
 
     check_dtree(dt_root);
 
+    DeviceState *pcie = qdev_new(TYPE_GPEX_HOST);
+    qdev_prop_set_uint32(pcie, "num-irqs", 0);
+    sysbus_realize_and_unref(SYS_BUS_DEVICE(pcie), &error_fatal);
+
     info->has_mte = kc_uses_mte(info->bootkc_f.buf);
 
     Object *cpuobj = object_new(ms->cpu_type);
-- 
